lowers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kotzwinkle/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kotzwinkle/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kotzwinkle/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kotzwinkle/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kotzwinkle/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kotzwinkle/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kotzwinkle/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kotzwinkle/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-28T17:46:56Z","updated_at":"2025-09-29T04:01:09Z","body":"> This is a limitation of embedded mode (since it's using IPC to send input to the child process).\n\nI see! Tested with the MRP and the project I originally encountered the issue with and can confirm that this is correct.\nI apologize if this is a known issue. If it's unavoidable in Mac while in embedded mode, would it makes sense to make note of the limitation in the documentation for set_custom_mouse_cursor?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3343973503/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3413345171","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110800#issuecomment-3413345171","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110800","id":3413345171,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Lc4OT","user":{"login":"angelFrog","id":7225901,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjU5MDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7225901?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/angelFrog","html_url":"https://github.com/angelFrog","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angelFrog/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angelFrog/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angelFrog/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angelFrog/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angelFrog/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angelFrog/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angelFrog/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angelFrog/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angelFrog/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-17T00:28:04Z","updated_at":"2025-10-17T00:28:04Z","body":"Apologies if I'm misreading the implications of the last couple comments, but this is not an embedded-only problem. It happens in windowed mode as well, both in my app and the MRP in the video above. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3413345171/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3413866118","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110800#issuecomment-3413866118","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110800","id":3413866118,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Le3aG","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-17T04:43:32Z","updated_at":"2025-10-17T04:43:32Z","body":">  It happens in windowed mode as well, both in my app and the MRP in the video above.\n\nThe video above is in embedded mode (toolbar is visible).","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3413866118/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3416247443","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110800#issuecomment-3416247443","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110800","id":3416247443,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Ln8yT","user":{"login":"angelFrog","id":7225901,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjU5MDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7225901?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/angelFrog","html_url":"https://github.com/angelFrog","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angelFrog/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angelFrog/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angelFrog/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angelFrog/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angelFrog/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angelFrog/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angelFrog/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angelFrog/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angelFrog/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-17T16:22:16Z","updated_at":"2025-10-17T16:22:16Z","body":"> The video above is in embedded mode (toolbar is visible).\n\nOh wow, learned something new. I thought embedded meant that it was running within the editor window rather than a separate window. Just moved to Godot two weeks ago and I've been running embedded all along without knowing it.\n\nHow does one know what embedded means? I can find very little mention of it online. A random YouTube video is the only place so far that says what it actually does. \n\nAlso, the cursor does change correctly in non-embedded mode, thank you 😊\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3416247443/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5500926159","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110800#issuecomment-5500926159","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110800","id":5500926159,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABR-F4zw","user":{"login":"bdreager","id":8732474,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MzI0NzQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8732474?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdreager","html_url":"https://github.com/bdreager","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdreager/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdreager/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdreager/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdreager/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdreager/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdreager/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdreager/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdreager/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdreager/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-01T21:52:14Z","updated_at":"2026-09-01T21:53:30Z","body":"I dug into this and I don't think it's an inherent limitation of the embedded-mode IPC - the cursor image does reach the editor process; the editor just never applies it until the mouse re-enters the game view. Read from current `master`:\n\n1. The embedded game's `DisplayServerMacOSEmbedded::cursor_set_custom_image()` (`platform/macos/display_server_macos_embedded.mm`) PNG-encodes the image and forwards it to the editor as `game_view:cursor_set_custom_image`.\n2. The editor receives it (`GameViewDebuggerMacOS::_msg_cursor_set_custom_image`, `platform/macos/editor/embedded_game_view_plugin.mm`) and calls `LayerHost::cursor_set_custom_image()` (`platform/macos/editor/embedded_process_macos.mm:327`), which **only stores it**:\n\n   ```cpp\n   void LayerHost::cursor_set_custom_image(const Ref<Image> &p_image, DisplayServerEnums::CursorShape p_shape, const Vector2 &p_hotspot) {\n       custom_cursors[p_shape] = CustomCursor(p_image, p_hotspot);\n   }\n   ```\n\n3. The stored images are pushed to the editor's real DisplayServer in exactly one place: the `LayerHost`'s `NOTIFICATION_MOUSE_ENTER` handler (same file, line 229). `NOTIFICATION_MOUSE_EXIT` clears them all.\n4. Cursor **shape** changes travel a separate, live path (`game_view:cursor_set_shape` -> `LayerHost::set_default_cursor_shape()` -> the editor viewport applies it on mouse motion).\n\nThat asymmetry -- images apply only on mouse-enter, shapes apply live -- reproduces every reported detail:\n\n- A `set_custom_mouse_cursor()` call in `_ready()` works: it arrives before the mouse first enters the game view, so the first mouse-enter applies it.\n- Any later call that replaces the image of the **currently active** shape has no visible effect until the mouse leaves the game view and comes back - exactly the \"have to move the cursor off and back on\" workaround in the OP.\n- Cursor changes driven by *shape* (hovering Controls with different `mouse_default_cursor_shape`) keep working, which makes the bug look intermittent.\n\nNon-embedded runs are unaffected: `DisplayServerMacOS::cursor_set_custom_image()` repaints via `[cursor set]` when `p_shape == cursor_shape`. I verified this with a standalone windowed test on 4.7.1-stable / macOS 26 (Apple Silicon) - replacing the active shape's image repaints immediately in a normal window, and only the embedded view shows the stale cursor.\n\nSo the fix looks small and editor-side only: track whether the mouse is currently over the `LayerHost` (paired with the same `MOUSE_ENTER`/`MOUSE_EXIT` notifications that already gate apply/clear) and apply an incoming image immediately when it is, e.g.:\n\n```cpp\nvoid LayerHost::cursor_set_custom_image(const Ref<Image> &p_image, DisplayServerEnums::CursorShape p_shape, const Vector2 &p_hotspot) {\n    custom_cursors[p_shape] = CustomCursor(p_image, p_hotspot);\n    if (mouse_over) { // set/cleared in NOTIFICATION_MOUSE_ENTER / _EXIT\n        DisplayServer::get_singleton()->cursor_set_custom_image(p_image, p_shape, p_hotspot);\n    }\n}\n```\n\nWindows/Linux embedding shouldn't need this since the game window drives its own cursor there.\n\n(PS please fix)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5500926159/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]